  "created": "2026-11-13T22:19:43.397Z",
  "description": "Optional external-CBLAS matrix-product backend for NumSharp. Reference the package and np.dot / np.matmul compute float32/float64 products through OpenBLAS instead of NumSharp's managed SIMD GEMM — faster on large matrices, and BIT-IDENTICAL to NumPy, via a route-for-route port of NumPy's two matrix-product dispatchers. Ships the prebuilt OpenBLAS binaries NumPy itself bundles (scipy-openblas 0.3.34.106.0, the version numpy 2.5.4 pins) as per-RID runtime assets, so the same binary is loaded on Windows, Linux and macOS with no Python installed; a locally discovered or explicitly named CBLAS still takes precedence. NumSharp.Core itself stays 100% managed C# with no native dependency: with this package absent, every kernel is NumSharp's own.",
  "iconFile": "numsharp.icon128.png",
  "id": "NumSharp.Interop.OpenBLAS",
  "isPrerelease": false,
  "lastEdited": "2026-11-13T22:26:26.043Z",
